cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Greek Clinical De-identification Benchmark: 500 synthetic discharge notes with arbitrated gold standard, scoring rules and system outputs"
abstract: >-
  First benchmark for clinical-text de-identification in Greek. 500 fully
  synthetic discharge notes (300 cardiac surgery, 100 cardiology, 100
  nephrology) generated by a frontier LLM under fixed hospital-layout
  skeletons; 7,937 must-redact identifier instances (dual full independent
  review, F1 = 0.998, arbitrated) and 6,747 must-survive clinical probes
  enabling measurement of over-redaction. Includes realistic PDF renderings,
  the complete scoring implementation, and the evaluated system's full outputs
  and per-decision results for two independent runs. Contains no real patient
  data.
